WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.956
"You want to ask Jev to help us spy on Morb?"

2
00:00:03.957 --> 00:00:09.248
Zann stared at Gliss, hardly believing his ears. "Are you kidding?"

3
00:00:09.249 --> 00:00:16.927
"Maybe Gliss is right," Perda said. "I know Jev's not your favorite person, Zann. But he's good at magic."

4
00:00:16.928 --> 00:00:21.277
"So what?" Zann said. "Lots of people are good at magic.

5
00:00:21.278 --> 00:00:24.247
We could ask your parents to help instead.

6
00:00:24.248 --> 00:00:28.032
Or maybe one of our teachers or the mayor."

7
00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:32.560
"It would take too long to explain everything to them," Gliss pointed out.

8
00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:36.686
"Besides, Jev will definitely do it if I ask him."

9
00:00:36.687 --> 00:00:41.423
Zann couldn't believe the girls were seriously thinking about going to Jev for help.

10
00:00:41.424 --> 00:00:45.267
He glanced at Darb, expecting his friend to be on his side.

11
00:00:45.268 --> 00:00:50.896
Darb had a thoughtful look. "Well, it's not a bad idea," he said.

12
00:00:50.897 --> 00:00:53.296
"Let's go find him," Perda said.

13
00:00:53.297 --> 00:00:59.209
Before Zann could say another word, the others were hurrying out of the Hollow.

14
00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.388
He had little choice but to follow.

15
00:01:01.389 --> 00:01:05.399
Soon they were all hiding in a clump of trees near Jev's house.

16
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.182
Jev was in the yard playing with his pet dragon, but they didn't dare call to him.

17
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:15.808
By now it was afternoon, and there were a lot more people around than there had been earlier.

18
00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:19.750
They all knew that Morb could be awake and lurking out there somewhere.

19
00:01:19.751 --> 00:01:26.750
"I wish we could just use a Summoning spell," Perda complained. "Living without magic is hard!"

20
00:01:26.751 --> 00:01:32.168
"I have an idea." Darb reached into his pocket for a pencil and paper.

21
00:01:32.169 --> 00:01:37.732
Scribbling a note, he held it out to Zing. "Take this to Jev, okay, buddy?"

22
00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:41.258
At first Zing didn't understand what Darb wanted.

23
00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:48.665
He tried to eat the note, and then he tried to roast it. But finally he figured it out.

24
00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:53.308
Jev looked up when the dragon flew at him. "Shoo! You'll scare Hazi."

25
00:01:53.309 --> 00:01:56.720
Then he blinked. "Wait a minute. Aren't you . . ."

26
00:01:56.721 --> 00:01:59.802
Zing whistled and dropped the note by Jev's feet.

27
00:01:59.803 --> 00:02:02.058
Jev grabbed the paper and read it.

28
00:02:02.059 --> 00:02:06.058
A second later he picked up his dragon and headed toward his house.

29
00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:11.955
"See?" Zann whispered. "He's ignoring the note! I told you he was—"

30
00:02:11.956 --> 00:02:16.823
"Wait," Gliss interrupted. "He's just putting his dragon inside."

31
00:02:16.824 --> 00:02:19.881
Sure enough, Jev was already hurrying toward them.

32
00:02:19.882 --> 00:02:23.111
When he heard what they wanted, he smirked at Zann.

33
00:02:23.112 --> 00:02:29.368
"Wow, it must be tough living with no magic like a Void all day, huh?" he said.

34
00:02:29.369 --> 00:02:32.657
"Especially for a snooty Red like you."

35
00:02:32.658 --> 00:02:37.671
"Will you help us, Jev?" Gliss asked, grabbing his arm. "Please?"

36
00:02:37.672 --> 00:02:43.202
Jev glanced down at her hand on his arm. "Um, sure," he said.

37
00:02:43.203 --> 00:02:46.885
"I was just kidding around. What do you want me to do?"

38
00:02:46.886 --> 00:02:51.037
It didn't take long for Jev to summon and send a spy fly to Morb.

39
00:02:51.038 --> 00:02:58.375
Zann watched the whole process, chafing silently at seeing his enemy do magic when he himself was

40
00:02:58.376 --> 00:03:04.031
powerless. "Thanks, Jev," Perda said. "Can you come find us in the Hollow when the spy fly

41
00:03:04.032 --> 00:03:08.485
returns?" "The Hollow?" Jev looked a little nervous. "Sure, I

42
00:03:08.486 --> 00:03:11.866
guess." Just then he noticed Gliss rubbing her

43
00:03:11.867 --> 00:03:15.052
stomach. "Are you hungry? I could conjure up some

44
00:03:15.053 --> 00:03:20.779
lunch." "That would be great!" Gliss said. "We haven't eaten since

45
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:26.227
yesterday." She talked him into conjuring up enough food for all of them, along with some fresh

46
00:03:26.228 --> 00:03:29.390
clothes. After that they left Jev and headed for the

47
00:03:29.391 --> 00:03:31.890
Hollow. When they got there, Zing

48
00:03:31.891 --> 00:03:37.449
whimpered. "I know, Zing," said Zann with a sigh. "I don't like being here

49
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.504
either. But it's safer than being out in the

50
00:03:40.505 --> 00:03:45.255
open." "How long do you think it will take the spy fly to get there and back?" Gliss

51
00:03:45.256 --> 00:03:53.716
asked. The others shrugged. Spy flies were very fast. Like message moths they could zap themselves long distances when

52
00:03:53.717 --> 00:03:59.749
necessary. But there was no way of telling how long it would take the little creature to find Morb and observe what he was

53
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:03.732
doing. By now Morb had probably woken up and left Zann's

54
00:04:03.733 --> 00:04:09.013
house. Zann pulled out Boz's diary. "Guess I'll start reading this while we're

55
00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:13.592
waiting. Maybe we can figure out whether it's still worth trying to get it to the

56
00:04:13.593 --> 00:04:18.395
palace." "Too bad none of us can do an advanced Restore spell yet," Perda

57
00:04:18.396 --> 00:04:21.818
said. "Maybe we could take the diary to Professor

58
00:04:21.819 --> 00:04:26.177
Liblow." "It was dangerous enough to leave the Hollow to find Jev," Darb

59
00:04:26.178 --> 00:04:29.403
said. "Morb and his trolls could be

60
00:04:29.404 --> 00:04:35.964
anywhere." "He's right," Zann agreed. "Besides, we don't even know if we need a Restore spell

61
00:04:35.965 --> 00:04:38.905
yet." Zann opened the diary to the first

62
00:04:38.906 --> 00:04:43.778
page. For a moment he just stared at his grandfather's familiar, loopy

63
00:04:43.779 --> 00:04:53.993
handwriting. Zann had always found it strange that Boz, a highly accomplished Magic Master, chose to record his life in such an old-fashioned and non-magical

64
00:04:53.994 --> 00:04:57.337
way. Pushing that thought aside, Zann started to

65
00:04:57.338 --> 00:05:00.176
read. The diary began before Zann was

66
00:05:00.177 --> 00:05:07.750
born. In fact, one of the earliest entries mentioned Zann's mother—Boz's daughter—meeting a handsome young explorer.

67
00:05:07.752 --> 00:05:11.453
"Dad," Zann murmured, tracing his father's name.

68
00:05:11.454 --> 00:05:15.336
It was tempting to read everything about his parents' early days together.

69
00:05:15.337 --> 00:05:17.852
He knew he didn't have time though.

70
00:05:17.853 --> 00:05:22.605
He skimmed over some entries about Boz's day-to-day life as a Magic Master.

71
00:05:22.606 --> 00:05:30.493
They were surprisingly boring, but then Zann saw pages filled with stories about his parents' explorations and adventures.

72
00:05:30.494 --> 00:05:35.752
"I can go back and read those later, when Boz is safe," he told himself.

73
00:05:35.753 --> 00:05:42.228
He tore his gaze away from a description of his own third birthday party and continued flipping through the diary.

74
00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:44.363
The next few pages were missing.

75
00:05:44.364 --> 00:05:59.629
When Zann turned to the next legible page, a familiar name jumped out at him; in bold, angry letters, his grandfather had scrawled "Morb."

